  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 48.5% accuracy, establishing RNA as the dominant modality over image (20.8% for resnet50). With only two completed experiments, we have high uncertainty about whether the RNA encoder choice matters. Question: config_004 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) changes only the RNA encoder from PCA (linear) to scvi (learned), keeping profile setting identical to config_001. This isolates the effect of representation learning. Why this is best: It is a single-variable comparison directly against config_001, making the result cleanly interpretable. If scvi substantially improves over PCA, it tells us representation learning is a high-leverage design axis and justifies further investment in scgpt and multimodal variants. If it does not, we can deprioritize encoder complexity and focus budget on profile/aggregation or fusion questions. This reduces the most critical uncertainty before committing to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

